.TH AIO 1 "August 2026" "aio 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aio, aio_bin, aiorewrite \- All-In-One Pygame Launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aio
.RI [ " \-\-cli | \-\-tui | \-\-gui | \-\-wui " \fR[\fI port \fR] " | \-\-tray " ]
.br
.B aio
.RI [ action ]
.RI [ argument ...]
.br
.B aio
.B \-h, \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aio
is a single-file application that discovers every public pygame game
(built-in examples, PyPI packages, GitHub repos and the awesome-pygame list)
and launches or installs any of them by name or listing number, through five
interfaces: CLI, TUI, GUI, WUI and system tray.
.PP
Run without arguments (or with
.B \-\-cli
) to list the numbered catalogue. Help is printed only for
.B \-h
or
.BR \-\-help .
The application runs from source
.RB ( aio.py )
or as a standalone native binary
.RB ( aio_bin ),
built with Cython and gcc.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B \-\-cli
Command line interface (the default). Lists the catalogue and runs actions.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Full-screen curses interface with per-source menus.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
tkinter window with one tab per source.
.TP
.BI "\-\-wui [" port ]
Web UI and JSON API; binds
.IR port
(default 8080) on localhost only.
.TP
.B \-\-tray
System tray icon and menu (pystray).
.SH CLI ACTIONS
.TP
.BR list " / " games " / " help
Print the numbered catalogue of all available games.
.TP
.BR launch " " name-or-number
Launch a game by name or listing number.
.TP
.BR install " " target
Install a game by name or number, a git repository URL, or a requirements
file (use
.B \-r
for an explicit requirements file).
.TP
.BR doctor
Print system status for the optional components.
.TP
.BR build " " system " " [ args ]
Build integration:
.IR cython ,
.IR cmake ,
.IR ninja ,
.IR meson
or
.IR cargo .
.TP
.BR jinja " " ...
Jinja2 templating helpers.
.TP
.BR docs " " format
Regenerate documentation:
.IR markdown ,
.IR html ,
.IR man ,
.IR doxygen
or
.IR all .
.TP
.BR hello " [" name ]
Echo demo.
.SH GAME SOURCES
The catalogue is assembled from four sources, continuously numbered
built-in 1-39, PyPI 40-386, GitHub 387-549 and awesome 550-561:
.TP
.B Built-in
pygame example games shipped with the installed pygame.
.TP
.B PyPI
pygame packages discovered by scanning the
.IR pypi.org/simple/
index.
.TP
.B GitHub
pygame repositories from the GitHub search API, top by stars.
.TP
.B Awesome
repositories from the curated awesome-pygame list.
.PP
Listings are cached in
.B pygame_games_cache.json
beside the executable (PyPI 7 days, GitHub 24 hours, awesome 7 days), so the
catalogue works offline after one online run.
.SH LAUNCH SEMANTICS
.TP
.B Built-in
Run
.B python -m pygame.examples.<name>.
.TP
.B PyPI
Ensure the package is installed, then run
.BR "python -m <pkg>" .
.TP
.B GitHub / awesome
Clone the repository, install its requirements, locate a runnable entry
point and execute it.
.TP
.B URL / local file
Clone-and-run a git URL, or run a local script directly.
.PP
Missing modules are auto-installed through pip and the launch is retried
once. Repositories with no runnable entry point (libraries such as
.B pygame_gui
or
.B pyscroll
) are reported as such; use
.B install
to install them as Python packages.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on operational errors, 130 when interrupted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B pygame_games_cache.json
Cached source listings (beside the executable).
.TP
.B venv/
Runtime environment used by the compiled binary.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aio-suite (7),
.BR aio-cli (1),
.BR aio-tui (1),
.BR aio-gui (1),
.BR aio-wui (1),
.BR aio-tray (1)
